# Structure
agents/
├── base_agent.py          # BaseAgent and HumanAgent classes
├── random_agent.py        # Random move agent (used as baseline)
├── vin_agent.py           # RLAgent — Actor-Critic RL agent
├── actor_critic.py        # CNN Actor-Critic neural network
├── intermediate_rewards.py # Shaped reward logic (threat detection)
├── human_train.py         # Interactive human-vs-agent training session
└── train.py               # Main training script + uses match.py for evaluation

game/
├── logic.py               # Core Gomoku game logic
├── gomoku_env.py          # RL environment wrapper (headless training)
├── board.py               # Pygame visual board
└── match.py               # Headless agent evaluation utilities

main.py                    # Entry point (play against agent or headless eval)


# Functionality - agent used actor-critic architecture trained with TD learning: 

Actor: CNN policy network that outputs a probability distribution over all board positions
Critic: Value head that estimates the expected return from a given board state
Reward shaping: Intermediate rewards from intermediate_rewards.py guide learning between terminal win/loss signals
Self-play: Agent trains against a frozen copy of itself, refreshed periodically
Entropy regularisation: Encourages exploration, decays over training

# Neural Network

Input: (1, board_size, board_size) — board from agents perspective (stones flipped to +1/-1)
  → Conv2d(1→32) + GroupNorm + ReLU
  → Conv2d(32→64) + GroupNorm + ReLU
  → Conv2d(64→64) + GroupNorm + ReLU
  → Flatten

Policy head → Linear → mask illegal moves → Softmax → action probabilities
Value head  → Linear(128) → Linear(1) → scalar value estimate

# Saved Models

Three model files are saved automatically during training.

File:                            Saved When:
gomoku_best_winrate_model.pth    Agent achieves a new highest winrate vs random
gomoku_best_reward_model.pth     Rolling average shaped reward improves (while winrate stays high)
gomoku_plateaued_model.pth       Shaped reward stabilises (std < 2.0 over last 5 evals) at high winrate


To choose which model to load at the start of training, set LOAD_MODEL at the top of train.py:

LOAD_MODEL = "gomoku_best_winrate_model.pth"  # or reward/plateaued

# Training

Standard Self-Play Training: 

run command: 
python -m agents.train

This runs up to max_episodes = 10000 episodes. Every 200 episodes it evaluates against a fresh RandomAgent over 200 games and prints winrate. 
Every 500 episodes the frozen self-play opponent is refreshed to a copy of the current agent.

Training progress output:

Episode 200 | total shaped reward this episode: 14.23
Results after 200 games:
  Agent 1 wins: 198 (99.0%)
  Agent 2 wins: 2 (1.0%)
Episode: 200, winrate vs random: 0.990
  -> New best winrate model saved (0.990)
Episode 500: Updated frozen opponent.

A winrate plot is shown at the end of training.

Human-in-the-Loop Training:

run command:


python -m agents.train --humantrain    # Load the winrate model (default)

OR

python -m agents.train --humantrain --model gomoku_plateaued_model.pth   # Load a specific model
python -m agents.train --humantrain --model gomoku_best_reward_model.pth


# Playing Against the Agent

run command:

python main.py

This opens the Pygame window. You play as Black (Player 1), the agent plays as Red (Player -1).
The agent loads from gomoku_best_model.pth by default (see main.py to change which model)
Click Start to begin, Reset to restart, Quit to exit


To play against a specific saved model, change the path in main.py:

if os.path.exists("gomoku_best_winrate_model.pth"):   # change to any of the three saved models
    rl_agent.load("gomoku_best_winrate_model.pth")   